31,2,,status,Shizue,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
32,2,,status,Rin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
33,2,,status,Jonathan,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
34,2,,status,Minako,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Shizue,,It seems our neighbors in the outer wards are quite isolated now that the buses have changed. It makes my heart ache.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"It is a significant gap. Furthermore, our physical doors close just as the remote demand peaks. We are missing people.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Rin,,I found out that we had outreach stops before and people loved them! But we also tried digitising photos and it was a total mess!,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"Fascinating. It appears we have a habit of returning capital funds while our operational lines bleed out. We are funding the ""thing"" but not the ""doing.""","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Minako,,"That matches my findings. We have volunteers with skills, but we have no staff trained to supervise them. We are adding tasks without adding capacity.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Jonathan, if the roads close but the halls stay open, perhaps we should not rely on our own vehicles to reach them.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Shizue, I agree. If the bus links are gone, the burden of travel is too high. We must bring the service to them.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Rin,,But we can't just do it randomly! The old records show that the partner-run groups worked because they didn't need us to do everything.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Rin, that is the logical path. If we use the endowment for the initial setup and avoid recurring operational traps, we might actually survive year two.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Minako,,"Only if the supervision is handled by the community. If the library staff are expected to certify tools or manage tradespeople, it will fail.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Shizue,,I feel we should choose a path that does not break when the weather turns or the bus schedule changes.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,A mobile service is risky if the roads close. Perhaps a satellite model or a community-led hub in those outer wards?,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Rin,,Yes! Like the groups from six years ago! They just did their own thing and it worked. Why can't we just do that again?,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"Because we must ensure the funding is shaped to support a partner, rather than a library-run operation that drains our running budget.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Minako,,I will support any proposal that shifts the technical burden away from the library staff and onto certified community partners.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,pass,Shizue,,Over,"{""forced"":false,""empty"":false}"
51,2,4,pass,Jonathan,,Over,"{""forced"":false,""empty"":false}"
