59,3,,status,Minako,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
60,3,1,talk,Shizue,,I am afraid the Mobile Branch is too fragile. The road closures and bus changes show us that we cannot rely on transport.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,"I agree. Option A is a risk. Option C, the Language Circles, could be hosted in the outer wards, bypassing the transport issue.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Rin,,Option D is just like the photo thing that failed six years ago! We shouldn't do it! Let's do the Language Circles!,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,Option A is a budget trap; the running costs for vehicles are already unstable. Option C is elegant because it leverages partners.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Minako,,"Option B requires tool certification and supervision, which we currently lack the staff to manage. Option C is the most sustainable for our roster.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Shizue,,"Option C feels very warm and inclusive. It brings people together in their own neighborhoods, where they feel safe.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,"It addresses the temporal gap too. If these circles happen in community spaces, they aren't bound by our nine o'clock lock-up.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Rin,,And it's like the partner groups that are still meeting! It's a proven shape! We just have to do it right this time!,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"From a financial perspective, Option C allows us to use the grant for facilitators while the community provides the space. It avoids the ""year two"" crash.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Minako,,"Exactly. It places the operational burden on the facilitators and partners, not on the library staff who are already overextended.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Shizue,,I feel very peaceful about this choice. It is a gentle way to expand without risking the stability of our services.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,It is the only option that truly solves the accessibility problem for the outer wards without creating a new dependency on unreliable transport.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Rin,,"I'm so glad we looked at the old stuff! If we didn't, we might have picked the digital portal and just made another mess!","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,It is a rare moment where the most compassionate choice is also the most logically sound. I am quite satisfied.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Minako,,I am convinced. Option C is the only proposal that aligns with our current staffing capabilities and skill sets.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
